      "status": "fixed",
      "status_notes": "http.client did not reject CR and LF characters in the proxy tunnel host and tunnel headers passed to set_tunnel(), allowing header injection into the CONNECT request. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/146211 (3.13 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/9e071c9b28c17f347f81b388a003d4eeb3c7a8dd), first released in CPython 3.13.14; see the advisory https://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/2IVPAEQWUJBCTQZEJEVTYCIKSMQPGRZ3/ and https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-1502. The DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.13 package carries a backport of that fix from 3.13.13-r3, made before the upstream 3.13.14 release; 3.13.14-r0 and later are built from CPython 3.13.14 or later (the version string in libpython3.13.so), which include it. Compared Lib/http/client.py in the python-3.13 package in every published build on x86_64 and aarch64 (3.13.12-r0 to 3.13.18-r4) with the file in the matching upstream CPython release: 3.13.12-r0 to 3.13.13-r2 ship the upstream file unchanged, without the control-character checks on the tunnel host and on each tunnel header name and value; 3.13.13-r3 to 3.13.13-r9 add it; 3.13.14-r0 and later ship the upstream 3.13.14 or later file, which has it (3.13.18-r4 adds further backported changes to that file and keeps the fix)."
    },
